Why vendored: the workload build is JDK-only (no Maven or Gradle) and must
work offline. The core workload stays free of third-party code
(docs/decisions.md #5); only workload-libs.jar runs against these jars,
named in its manifest's Class-Path, not copied into it. `mage
workloadLibsBuild` checks the SHA-256s above before compiling.

Why this version: httpclient5 5.6.5 is the newest release at least two
weeks old on the fetch date; the core versions are the ones its pom pins.
The classic client is Java 8 bytecode, so the smoke run loads it on every
JDK the agent supports (decision #29: 17+).

To update: download the jars of the new version (and the versions its pom
pins) from Maven Central, compare each SHA-1 with the published .sha1,
replace the jars and license files, and update the versions, the hashes
here and libsJars in magefile_libs.go in the same commit.
